# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Suggested team handles
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This is a one-maintainer portfolio repository, so the only *valid* owner today
# is @Francisco-cor. The handles below describe how a 3-5 person team would split
# the same paths; they do not exist as GitHub teams yet.
#
# When an org team is created (Settings → Access → Teams → New team), replace
# the matching `@Francisco-cor` rule with the team handle, e.g.:
#   /services/productos/  @your-org/erp-catalogo
#
# GitHub silently ignores CODEOWNERS entries that point to unknown users or
# teams, which would leave a path unprotected. Keep the fallback `*` rule and
# only add a team after it exists in the organization.
#
# Suggested split:
#   @org/erp-catalogo   → services/productos, services/stock (inventory domain)
#   @org/erp-pedidos    → services/ordenes, services/gateway (orders + BFF)
#   @org/erp-platform   → terraform, scripts, .github/workflows (infra/CI)
#   @org/erp-docs       → docs, README.md, CONTRIBUTING.md
#   @org/erp-frontend   → frontend, nginx (edge + static dashboard)

